3. How to implement incremental data load using Python

Answer:

“Incremental loading means processing only new or updated data instead of full loads.

Common approaches:
	•	Using timestamps (e.g., last_updated)
	•	Using primary keys or IDs
	•	Maintaining a checkpoint file or metadata table

Example approach:
	•	Store the last processed timestamp
	•	Fetch data where updated_at > last_timestamp
	•	Update the timestamp after processing

This improves efficiency and reduces processing cost.”

